                            The Vietnam Scaling up Energy Efficiency Project (VSUEE) is financed by the Green Climate Fund (GCF) with a total of USD 11.3 million through the World Bank.<br><br>
                            The project includes two components: Component 1 - Risk Sharing Facility (RSF) and Component 2 - Technical Assistance.<br><br>
                            The project is implemented from March of 2022 to January of 2026 throughout the country. The Ministry of Industry and Trade is the project governing agency, responsible for the project's results.

                        </p>
                        <a href="/gioi-thieu/c76/introduction.html" class="btn-green mt30">View More</a>
